          %h2#idea Idea
          %h3#general General
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+theory"} Kaluza-Klein theory
            where an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Maxwell+theory"} Einstein-Maxwell theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            is modeled by a configuration of pure Einstein
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravity
            in dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            %em Kaluza-Klein monopole
            is a configuration of gravity in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            which in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            looks like a magnetic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sorkin83"}> Sorkin 83
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GrossPerry83"} Gross-Perry 83
          %h3#in_supergravity In supergravity
          %p
            This situation is of particular interest in the reduction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-brane"} MK6-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            charge under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+between+M-theory+and+type+IIA+string+theory"} duality between M-theory and type IIA string theory
          %p
            The
            %em Kaluza-Klein monopole
            (
            %a{:href => "#HanKoh85"}> Han-Koh 85
            ) is one type of solution of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 11
                      %mo −
                      %mn 5
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_4\times \mathbb{R}^{11-5,1}
            of Euclidean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Taub-NUT+spacetime"} Taub-NUT spacetime
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Minkowski+spacetime"} Minkowski spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            this looks like a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monopole"} monopole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
            see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#IMSY98"} IMSY 98, section 9
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a{:href => "#Asano00"} Asano 00, section 3
          %p
            Upon
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            on a 6-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            completely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+brane"} wrapping
            the fiber, the KK-monopole in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            becomes the KK-monopole in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+supergravity"} 5d supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            in 4d, incarnated as a D0/D6 bound state (e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Nelson93"} Nelson 93
