                    (e.g.
                    = succeed ")" do
                      %a{:href => "Kaluza-Klein+monopole#Asano00"} Asano 00, Sect. 3
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            (For the moment the following is all about the KK-monopoles in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11d+supergravity"} 11d supergravity
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %h3#NearHorizonGeometry Far-horizon geometry
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/far+horizon+geometry"} far horizon geometry
            of coincident MK6-branes.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+tensor"} metric tensor
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            coincident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopoles"} KK-monopoles
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            in the limit that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi th
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell_{th} \coloneqq N \ell_P \to 0
            is
          #eq:SmallNMK6.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi MK
                      %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mn 6
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi sin
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi φ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi cos
                  %mi θ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mi ϕ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{MK6}
                  \\;=\;
                  g_{\mathbb{R}^{6,1}}
                  +
                  (d y)^2
                  +
                  y^2
                  \\big(
                  (d \theta)^2
                  +
                  (\sin \theta)^2 (d \varphi)^2
                  +
                  (\cos \theta)^2 (d \phi)^2
                  \\big)
          %p subject to the identification
          #eq:OrbifoldIdentificationForKKMonopole.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ∼
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi φ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi N
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\varphi, \phi)
                  \\;\sim\;
                  (\varphi, \phi) + (2\pi/N ,2\pi/N)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is equation (47) in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#IMSY98"} IMSY 98
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi g
                          %mi YM
                          %mrow
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 3
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mfrac
                      %mi N
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mi π
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mn 3
                        %msub
                          %mi ℓ
                          %mi P
                    %mo )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≫
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U/\left(\frac{N}{g^{2/3}_{YM}}\right)
                  \\;=\;
                  U/\left(\frac{N}{(2\pi)^{4/3} \ell_P}\right)
                  \\;\gg\;
                  1
          %p
            from a few lines above. Inserting this condition into the definition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi y
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ≔
                  %mn 2
                  %mi N
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y^2 \coloneqq 2 N \ell^3_P U
            right above (47) shows that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi y
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %mi N
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℓ
                            %mi P
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 2
                          %mi π
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 4
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mn 3
                          %msup
                            %mi N
                            %mn 2
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℓ
                            %mi P
                            %mn 2
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %munder
                            %munder
                              %mrow
                                %mo (
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mrow
                                  %mo (
                                  %mfrac
                                    %mi N
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mn 2
                                      %mi π
                                      %msup
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                        %mrow
                                          %mn 4
                                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                          %mn 3
                                      %msub
                                        %mi ℓ
                                        %mi P
                                  %mo )
                                %mo )
                              %mo ⏟
                            %mrow
                              %mo ≫
                              %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  y^2
                  \&amp; =
                  2 N \ell^3_P U
                  \\\
                  \&amp; =
                  2(2\pi)^{-4/3} N^2 \ell_P^2
                  \\;
                  \\underset{
                  \\gg 1
                  }{
                  \\underbrace{
                  \\left(U/\left(\frac{N}{ (2 \pi)^{4/3} \ell_P}\right)\right)
                  }}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            hence that the distance
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            from the locus of the MK6-brane is large in units of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi th
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msqrt
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 3
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\ell_{th} \;=\; \sqrt{2} (2\pi)^{-2/3} N \ell_P
                  \\,.
          %p
            The identification
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:OrbifoldIdentificationForKKMonopole"} (2)
            means that this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+cone"} metric cone
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 6
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{6,1} \times \left( \mathbb{R}^4/(\mathbb{Z}_N)\right)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"}
              A-type
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE-singularity"} ADE-singularity
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi φ
                  %mi sin
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi w
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi ϕ
                  %mi cos
                  %mi θ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  v \;\coloneqq\; y \, e^{i \varphi} \sin \theta
                  \\;\;\;
                  w \;\coloneqq\; y \, e^{i \phi} \cos \theta
          %p
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 4
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^4 \simeq \mathbb{C}^2
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SmallNMK6"} (1)
            becomes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi MK
                      %mn 6
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mi v
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mi v
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %mi w
                  %mi d
                  %mover
                    %mi w
                    %mo ¯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  g_{MK6}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  d v d \overline v
                  +
                  d w d \overline w
          %p
            and which exhibit the identification
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:OrbifoldIdentificationForKKMonopole"} (2)
            as indeed that of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} A-type
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_N
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Asano00"} Asano 00, around (18)
          %h3#RelationToTheD6Brane Relation to the D6-brane in type IIA string theory
          %p
            Under the relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+IIA+superstring+theory"} type IIA superstring theory
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+orbifold"} ADE orbifold
            of the 11d KK-monopole corresponds to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            combined with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/O6-planes"} O6-planes
            (
            %a{:href => "#Townsend95"}> Townsend 95, p. 6
            ,
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01, p. 17-18
            see also e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BerglundBrandhuber02"} Berglund-Brandhuber 02, around p. 15
          %p
            By (
            %a{:href => "#Townsend95"}> Townsend 95, (1)
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sen97c"} Sen 97c (1)-(4)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            describing the KK-monopole lift of a plain single D6 brane is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 6
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{6,1}\times \mathbb{R}^3\times S^1
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+tensor"} metric tensor
            away from the origin of the
            = succeed "-factor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msubsup
                    %mi s
                    %mn 11
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi t
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi d
                  %msubsup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 6
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi d
                  %msubsup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 11
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mi d
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d s_{11}^2 =
                  \- d t^2
                  + d s_{\mathbb{R}^6}^2
                  + (1+\mu/r) d s_{\mathbb{R}^3}^2
                  + (1+ \mu/r)^{-1} (d x^{11} - A_i d x^i)^2
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi i
                      %mi d
                      %msup
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = A_i d x^i
                is any 3-form on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
                satisfying
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi ℝ
                              %mn 3
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mo ⋆
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %mi μ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi r
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathbb{R}^3} A = \star d (1-\mu/r)
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                denotes the distance in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
                from the origin.
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
                of the monopole.
          %div{:style => "float:left;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/TaubNUT.png", :width => "300"}/
          %p
            Away from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\} \in \mathbb{R}^3
            this gives a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            measured by the integral of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi d
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_0 \coloneqq d A
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-brane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sphere"} sphere
            surrounding the singular locus in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 - \{0\}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric-magnetic+duality"} electric-magnetic duality
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-branes"} D0-branes
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            (due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-dual+higher+gauge+theory"} self-duality
            of the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-field"} RR-field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \in \mathbb{R}^3
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            is located.
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#AcharyaGukov04"} Acharya-Gukov 04
          %p
            Notice that the circle bundle away from its degeneration locus as a bundle over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^3 -\{0\}
            is necessarily of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 3
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^3 \to S^2
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
            (see also
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahMaldacenaVafa00"} Atiyah-Maldacena-Vafa 00, p. 10
          %p
            Discussion as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} A-type ADE singularity
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Sen97c"}> Sen 97c, section 2
            ). Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+singularity"} D-type singularities
            and hence D6-branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientifolds"} orientifolds
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#Sen97c"}> Sen 97c ,section 3
            ). Discussion as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            of the
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the M-theory circle fibers is in (
            %a{:href => "#Townsend95"}> Townsend 95, p. 6
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahWitten01"} Atiyah-Witten 01, pages 17-18
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"} orbifold
            singularity but really a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conical+singularity"} conical singularity
          %blockquote
            %p#Witten01OnConicalSingularity
              Chiral fermions arise when the locus of A−D−E singularities passes through isolated points at which X has an isolated conical singularity that is not just an orbifold singularity (
              %a{:href => "#Witten01"}> Witten 01, p. 2
              ).
          %p
            Discussion dealing carefully with the perspective where the locus of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-brane"} D6-brane
            is not remived:
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GaillardSchmude09"} Gaillard &amp; Schmude 09
          %p
            For more on this see at
            %em
              %a{:href => "D6-brane#RelationToOtherBranes"} D6-brane – Relation to other branes
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+lift+of+gauge+enhancement+on+D6-branes"} M-theory lift of gauge enhancement on D6-branes
          %h3#relation_to_the_d7brane_in_type_iib_string_theoryftheory Relation to the D7-brane in type IIB string theory/F-theory
          %p
