          %h3#OtherBraneCharges Other Brane charges (?)
          %p
            %a{:href => "#Hull97"} Hull 1997
            argued (around equation 2.12) that the KK-monopole in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/11-dimensional+supergravity"} 11-dimensional supergravity
            is the object which carries the 6-form charge
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincar%C3%A9+duality"} Poincaré dual
            to the time-component of the 5-form charge of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            as appearing in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+super+Lie+algebra"} M-theory super Lie algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 10
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 5
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 10
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mn 6
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 10
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\wedge^5 (\mathbb{R}^{10,1})^\ast
                  \\simeq
                  \\wedge^5 (\mathbb{R}^{10})^\ast
                  \\oplus
                  \\wedge^6 \mathbb{R}^{10}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (An analogous relation identifies the time-component of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"} M2-brane
            charge with the charge of the
            = succeed "," do
